{"term":"protocol","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:355133f5ab63510815","definition":"The minutes, or official record, of a negotiation or transaction; especially a document drawn up officially which forms the legal basis for subsequent agreements based on it.","example":"Another account says that, on the morning of the 31st of May, the king delivered to the prince-royal the crown, the sceptre, and the key of his treasure and gave him his blessing. The privy-counsillor Vockerodt drew up at his desire a protocol of the transaction.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"countable, historical, uncountable","wordFamily":["Address Resolution Protocol","application protocol data unit","bonding protocol","Budwig protocol","Chicago Protocol","cryptoprotocol","File Transfer Protocol","immunoprotocol","Internet Protocol","interprotocol","intraprotocol","Kyoto Protocol","layer 2 tunnelling protocol","layer two tunnelling protocol","metaprotocol","Milwaukee protocol","multiprotocol","Needham-Schroeder protocol","Newman-Goldfarb protocol","Otway-Rees protocol","preprotocol","protocolary","protocolic","protocoligorically","protocolist","protocolization","protocolize","protocol sentence","protocol stack","pseudoprotocol"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protocol#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:807bf2b52c20867064","definition":"An official record of a diplomatic meeting or negotiation; later specifically, a draft document setting out agreements to be signed into force by a subsequent formal treaty.","example":"The terms of this protocol formed the basis for the Treaty of London signed by the British, French and Russian governments on 6 July 1827.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["Address Resolution Protocol","appli